From a417f11e67805380be9e8a4b35e76b70effd22b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 14:01:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] freedreno/a2xx: WAIT_FOR_IDLE at start of
 fd2_emit_restore

Per Gemini-AI analysis of the long-standing post-LSM-kill state leak
on Adreno 220 / HP TouchPad: mainline freedreno does not have the
context-isolation that legacy KGSL achieves via PM4_CONTEXT_UPDATE /
PM4_LOAD_CONSTANT_CONTEXT (both include implicit pipeline drains and
neither can be used safely on a2xx in mainline because the hardware
shadow-memory mechanism causes GPU hangs).

fd2_emit_restore is the equivalent state-restore path, called at every
batch start. It writes a long sequence of registers (RBBM_PM_OVERRIDE,
TP0_CHICKEN, CP_INVALIDATE_STATE, SQ_VS_CONST/PS_CONST, VGT_INDX_OFFSET,
PA_SU_SC_MODE_CNTL, VFD/VPC equivalents, etc.) but starts immediately
without draining the pipeline. With one shared GPU context across all
DRM clients on this driver, the previous client (luna-surfacemanager)
may still be retiring work touching some of those same blocks when the
new client's emit_restore writes start coming through. Result: races
that produce visible state-pollution symptoms even though the user-
draw cmdstream the next client emits is byte-identical to a cold-boot
run (verified via cffdump diff).

Add an explicit CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE at the very entry of fd2_emit_restore
to drain whatever the previous DRM client left in flight before we
start writing context state. Cheap (one CP packet, no perf cost when
the pipeline is already empty), surgical (only fires once per batch
start, not per draw), and matches the "context-switch firewall"
pattern that PM4_CONTEXT_UPDATE achieves implicitly in KGSL.

Targets the residual post-LSM kmscube bugs (gears ghost-quad,
intermittent face fade-in/out, glmark2 texture-broken-on-first-cycle)
that survived patches 0038 (mark all state dirty after GMEM tile
setup/resolve/sysmem_prep) and 0039 (TC L2 invalidate at batch start,
since superseded by Mesa's existing per-draw L2 invalidate at
fd2_draw.c:246).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
(cherry picked from commit f867516997b1a866910c107c7f5a327dabaef510)
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
index 05a69b12a71..8b866887818 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_emit.c
@@ -432,6 +432,30 @@ fd2_emit_restore(struct fd_context *ctx, struct fd_ringbuffer *ring)
       OUT_RING(ring, CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT);
    }
 
+   /*
+    * Drain the pipeline before issuing the state-restore register writes.
+    * Without an explicit WFI here, the writes can race the previous
+    * client's in-flight retirement. This is what KGSL effectively does
+    * via PM4_CONTEXT_UPDATE / PM4_LOAD_CONSTANT_CONTEXT (both of which
+    * include implicit pipeline drains and which mainline freedreno
+    * cannot use safely on a2xx because the hardware shadow-memory
+    * mechanism causes hangs).
+    *
+    * Mainline mainstream a2xx already has a CP_WAIT_REG_EQ on
+    * RBBM_STATUS later in this function, but that fires AFTER the
+    * VGT_VERTEX_REUSE_BLOCK_CNTL / RBBM_PM_OVERRIDE / TP0_CHICKEN /
+    * SQ_VS_CONST / SQ_PS_CONST / etc. writes have already gone through.
+    * The previous client's work could be touching some of those very
+    * same blocks while we write them.
+    *
+    * Adding an explicit drain here is cheap (one CP packet, no perf
+    * cost when the pipeline is already empty) and aligned with the
+    * "context-switch firewall" pattern Gemini's analysis recommends
+    * for state-pollution issues that survive cmdstream-byte-identity.
+    */
+   OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE, 1);
+   OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000000);
+
    if (is_a20x(ctx->screen)) {
       OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A2XX_RB_BC_CONTROL, 1);
       OUT_RING(ring, A2XX_RB_BC_CONTROL_ACCUM_TIMEOUT_SELECT(3) |
-- 
